evelopment and progression of human cancer</article-title><source>Virchows Arch</source><volume>446</volume><fpage>475</fpage><lpage>82</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15856292</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-btt-1-229"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Duursma</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Agami</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Ras interference as cancer therapy</article-title><source>Semin Cancer Biol</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>267</fpage><lpage>73</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14563121</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-btt-1-229"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Engel</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaklamani</surname><given-names>VG</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>HER2-positive breast cancer: current and future treatment strategies</article-title><source>Drugs</source><volume>67</volume><fpage>1329</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17547474</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-btt-1-229"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Esteva</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Valero</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Booser</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Phase II study of weekly docetaxel and trastuzumab for patients with HER-2-overexpressing metastatic breast cancer</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>1800</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11919237</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-btt-1-229"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Geyer</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>Forster</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindquist</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Lapatinib plus capecitabine for HER2-positive advanced breast cancer</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><volume>355</volume><fpage>2733</fpage><lpage>43</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17192538</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15-btt-1-229"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henson</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Gibson</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Villanueva</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Increased expression of Mcl-1 is responsible for the blockage of TRAIL-induced apoptosis mediated by EGF/ErbB1 signaling pathway</article-title><source>J Cell Biochem</source><volume>89</volume><fpage>1177</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12898516</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b16-btt-1-229"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Herbst</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Review of epidermal growth factor receptor biology</article-title><source>Int J Radiat Oncol Biol Phys</source><volume>59</volume><fpage>21</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15142631</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b17-btt-1-229"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hynes</surname><given-names>NE</given-names></name><name><surname>Lane</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>ERBB receptors and cancer: the complexity of targeted inhibitors</article-title><source>Nat Rev Cancer</source><volume>5</volume><fpage>